Hi,

I have another issue when using this exactly same dataset (so tdf and edf files are the same I provided earlier). I have run ten different models from which the results are extracted in the table below. I provide also the R code in a separate file.

Looking at the table it seems strange that the density increases with 30% just because the sigma is allowed to be sex specific. I am comparing here the top model with the one with time dependent p0 and constant sigma. Also it feels odd that sigma is not really different between the sexes even though the models with sex-specific sigmas appear to be on the top based on AIC values. Also the sigmas are very different between models where sigma is sex dependent and where it’s not.

I have trying to figure out with my supervisor what is wrong here? There shouldn't be any simple copy-paste erros..

And how to interpret the change in psi parameter between these models?

best regards,

Jenni

