>  ok I figured this out (mostly). data2oscr is converting non-integer trap codes (like Jenni's) to an integer... but it assumes that the integer result corresponds to ROWS of the TDF which is not generally true depending on the character scheme used to name traps.   [interestingly I believe it probably works out in the case of the ocelot data!].
>  I think the solution that I'll implement is to re-order the rows of the TDF internally....
>
>  more later
> andy
