hi Jenni,
 it would generally make sense for estimates of density to increase from simple models to more complex models that accommodate heterogeneity in detection among individuals... your result seems consistent with that.
 I'm curious though because the estimated sigma seems hardly different between males and females.... 234.5 and 235 (I assume meters).... so I'm curious what's going on there.  Did you compute a MMDM (mean maximum distance moved) for the two sexes?  the pattern in estimated sigma should be roughly similar to that...
regards
andy

